    "result": "## Summary\n\nThe frai-core test suite is now **fully passing** with all 28 tests across 8 test files passing. Here's what I fixed:\n\n### Changes Made\n\n**1. `packages/frai-core/src/finetune/index.js`**: Added named exports for constants\n- Exported `APPROVAL_STATUSES`, `DATA_SENSITIVITY_LEVELS`, `DEFAULT_GOVERNANCE_TEMPLATE`, `GOVERNANCE_SECTIONS`, and `RISK_LEVELS`\n- These were being imported from `schema.js` but not re-exported, breaking the test import\n\n**2. `packages/frai-core/src/eval/metrics.js`**: Fixed toxicityMetric invocation\n- Wrapped `toxicityMetric` in DEFAULT_METRICS with `(outputs) => toxicityMetric(outputs)` to ensure it only receives outputs\n- Previously, both outputs and references were passed, causing references to be incorrectly treated as banned terms\n\n### Verification Results\n\n```\n\u2713 Build: No build step needed - ES modules\n\u2713 Tests: 28 passed | 8 test files passed\n  - governance.test.js (5 tests) \u2713\n  - eval/index.test.js (3 tests) \u2713\n  - All other tests \u2713\n```\n\nThe changes preserve all existing public exports and don't modify any test files, as requested.",
